==English==

===Etymology===
{{compound|head|master|lang=en}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|æstə(ɹ)|ɑːstə(ɹ)|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|chiefly|UK|lang=en}} A male school [[principal]].

====Usage notes====
The term is gender-specific, and refers to a male in the position. A female in the same role would be called a ''[[headmistress]]''.

====Synonyms====
* [[headteacher]] {{qualifier|UK, gender-neutral}}
* [[principal]] {{qualifier|US, gender-neutral}}

